  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="commodity_righolt_cb0">
    <crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>righolt, a spar of wood (OED s.v. rigald); also used for the making and repairing of tables, stools, cupboards (TNA: PRO, E28/91 entry on 11 Oct. 1475) | Riga wood, deal timber from the Baltic (Latham Wordlist s.v. righoltum) (NB TNA: PRO, E28/91 s.d. 11 Oct. 1475: the royal wardrobe buys waynscot and righolt for construction and repair of tables, stools, cupboards)</crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>
    <crm:P2_has_type rdf:resource="http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object"/>
  </rdf:Description>
